cellPad: Enter/Esc confirm and go back in menus (fps layout), from a host menu query.

On a PC Enter confirms and Esc goes back in a menu, and Esc pauses in the game. Resistance 3's menus confirm with CROSS
and go back with CIRCLE, and START there means "player 2 join"; only the "Press START" screen and the game itself want
START. The keyboard cannot tell these apart, so the host says: cellPad_set_menu_query(fn) registers a function that is
non-zero while the title shows a menu (the host reads the game's own flags for it). In a menu Enter = CROSS and
Esc = CIRCLE; elsewhere both press START. A key keeps the button it got when it went down until it is released: Esc
pauses, the pause menu opens while the key is still held, and it must not become CIRCLE there and close the menu again
(the same for Enter starting a level). Without a query nothing changes.

Test: libs/input/tests/test_pad_keyboard_fps.c test_menu_keys (both keys in and out of a menu, held across a context
change, no hook). Scripted run: the host's query follows the title screen, menus, pause and gameplay.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

